Subject: [PATCH] web-app: Export Chat entry in the three-dot menu (zip built
 fork-side)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Telegram-style chat export: an 'Export Chat' entry in the main-view
three-dot menu downloads the open chat as one zip (standalone html
viewer that looks like the message list, messages.txt, messages.json,
media/, and a webxdc manifest so the zip doubles as a viewer app).

Only the entry and a progress dialog with cancel live here. The dialog
calls window.__slothfulExportChat(chatId, options), registered by
slothfulchat-web's packages/web-app/src/chat-export.ts, which fetches
the messages, collects the media, inlines the app css and writes the
zip — none of it touches React, so none of it is rebased against
upstream. The dialog passes along what only the frontend bundle knows:
the hashed css-module class names the viewer reuses (message bubbles,
footer, reactions) and a moment formatter in the user's locale for
messages.txt and the filename. Cancel aborts an AbortSignal. New
strings live in _untranslated_en.json.

web-app: chat export confirm dialog (exclusions + date range)

Export Chat now opens a confirm dialog before running: it explains what
the export contains and — per review of what the app shows that an
export cannot carry — states that read receipts, full HTML e-mail
contents and webxdc app contents are not included. Optional From/Until
date fields (inclusive, local time) are passed to
window.__slothfulExportChat as unix-second bounds; the fork-side
exporter applies them to the viewer, messages.json, messages.txt and
the bundled media alike.

New strings live in _untranslated_en.json.
